# The lava caverns: Act 2, level 1
# DRAFT by Claude for Matt to mark up (2026-10-25). Started before G2 passes,
# at Matt's word: the plan is provisional until he and the kids have played
# the rebuilt wall. Nothing is built from it until he approves it. The
# questions it raises are at the foot (*Before building*).
#
# Act 2 as two levels (Claude's proposal): this one, from the castle's
# undercroft down to the lair door, and level 2, the mine and the dragon's
# lair. Today's six rooms become sections: the mouth is beat 2, the geyser
# shaft beats 4 and 8, the causeway beat 6, the tide beat 7. The mine and
# the lair are level 2's, on a sheet of their own.
#
# Act 1 climbed. This level goes down, five floors to one, into the heat.
# The geysers are how you come back up, which is what most loops are.
ideas: the ferry, the geyser, the throw from a falling floor, the tide
carried in from Act 1: throw and catch, a sword in wood is a ledge, the switch a sword holds, the floor that holds once, bats on ladders

## 1. The undercroft  [breather]  floor 5
Through the castle gate and down a stair cut in the rock. Masonry gives way
to basalt. The first glow comes up from below, with the sound of it. Timber
props and beams hold up the roof, so wood is still something to look for.
brazier: here

## 2. The first ferry  [introduce: the ferry]  floor 5
A basalt slab riding back and forth over lava too wide to jump. Nothing
alive. Wait for it, step on, ride, step off. The banks are wide, so a step
taken early or late lands on rock.
can kill you: the lava
note: a fall costs the walk from 1, which is a few steps.

## 3. The first slabs  [introduce: the throw from a falling floor]  floor 5
A line of slabs that give way a moment after you land, over a dry pit. A
bat circles above the far half. Throw from a slab and keep moving: the
sword comes home to you wherever you are now. The pit under the slabs has
no lava in it, so a fall costs nothing but the way back up, which is 4.
can kill you: the bat

## 4. The vent  [introduce: the geyser]  floors 4 to 5
The pit floor under 3. A jet comes out of dry rock on its own clock and
throws you back up to the undercroft's ledge. Missing it costs a wait.
loop: up the jet to the brazier at 1

## 5. The ferry under the bat  [develop: the ferry]  floor 4
A longer crossing, lower down, with a bat working the air over the
ferry's path. Standing still is not on offer. Throw from the moving
ferry, and a miss comes home to wherever the ferry has carried you, which
may be under the bat.
can kill you: the bat, the lava
brazier: on the far bank

## 6. The causeway  [develop: the throw from a falling floor]  floor 4
Today's causeway: two lines of slabs over lava, a bat at body height over
the second. Throw from a slab before it goes and be on the next one for
the catch. A miss you are not there for lands behind you.
can kill you: the bat, the lava

## 7. The low passage  [introduce: the tide]  floor 3
Today's tide, shorter. A low passage between rock refuges. The lava lies
under the passage floor, comes up over it, stands, and goes back down.
Cross a stretch while it is low and be on the next refuge before it comes.
The first stretch is short and the brazier is at its mouth, so a misjudged
tide costs one stretch. A chest on the last refuge, after two bat fights.
can kill you: the tide
brazier: at the passage mouth

## 8. The geyser well  [develop: the geyser]  floors 3 to 5
A jet that comes out of lava, not rock: step in while it runs, or step in
the lava. A bat at the well's top ledge. Throw at it from the well floor,
then ride the jet. A sword that misses comes home to you at the top, not
at the floor you threw from.
can kill you: the bat, the lava
loop: from the top ledge, a ladder down to the brazier at 7

## 8a. The sword graveyard  [pocket]  floor 5
Along the top ledge from the well, a cave floor scattered with swords left
by whoever came before and did not come back for theirs. Atmosphere, as
`LEVELS.md` has it. One of them is a fourth sword (see *Before building*:
the others must not read as pickups).

## 9. The scorpion's dock  [twist: the ferry]  floor 3
A ferry docks at a bank a scorpion patrols, and it faces the dock as you
arrive. The answer that worked (ride, step off) puts you against its
armoured front. Stay on, ride past the dock to the ferry's far stop over
the lava, and throw back at its back as it walks away from the edge.
can kill you: the scorpion, the lava
brazier: on the dock, once it is yours

## 10. The quick bridge  [twist: the throw from a falling floor]  floor 3
Slabs that go faster than a throw comes home, with a bat at the far end at
body height. Thrown from a slab, the sword is still out when the slab
drops. The throw has to start from the bank, and you run while it flies:
the catch is on the far bank, or on the last slab if you are quick.
can kill you: the bat, the lava

## 11. The tide gallery  [develop: the tide]  floor 3
A longer passage, and a bat works the air over its middle refuge. The
refuge you wait the tide out on is inside the bat's box. Throw from the
refuge before the tide comes and the catch is yours to wait for, or cross
two stretches on one low tide and skip the refuge, which is tight.
can kill you: the bat, the tide

## 12. The forge hall  [breather]  floor 3
An old working: anvils, a quench trough of lava, chains on the walls. From
below, a sound you will hear again at the lair. A chest, because the next
stretch is the hardest.
brazier: here

## 13. The flue  [twist: the geyser]  floors 3 to 1
The way down is a geyser shaft. Every jet so far was a lift. This one is
in the way. Drop between eruptions and get out sideways at the foot before
the next one, or it throws you back up to the forge hall's floor and you
try again.
note: thrown back up is the cost. Nothing at the foot kills you.

## 14. The rising shaft  [twist: the tide]  floors 1 to 2
Out of the flue into the foot of a tall shaft, and the tide comes up it.
Every tide so far was waited out on a refuge. This one rises past every
refuge in the shaft, so waiting kills. Climb: ladders and ledges, no
enemy, only the clock.
can kill you: the tide
brazier: at the top

## 15. The ferry gate  [combine: the ferry + the switch a sword holds]  floor 2
A gate on the ferry's far bank, and its switch a timber block on a pillar
in the middle of the lava, out of reach from either bank. A flat throw from
the ferry as it passes is the only one that reaches it. The gate rises and
stays up while the sword holds it. Ride across, go through, recall it from
the far side, and the gate drops behind you.
can kill you: the lava
loop: past the gate, a passage back to the brazier at 14

## 16. The roost over the slabs  [combine: the throw from a falling floor + bats on ladders]  floors 1 to 2
A line of falling slabs ends at the foot of a ladder, with a bat circling
its top half. The slabs will not wait for a fight, so the throw is from
the ladder, and the slab you came over is gone. A miss comes home to you
on the ladder. Drop off and the floor below is lava.
can kill you: the bat, the lava
brazier: at the ladder's top

## 17. The planks over the tide  [combine: the tide + the floor that holds once]  floor 1
Planks over a tide passage that hold once. Going out they hold. The way on
is down through them, onto the passage floor, and the drop is safe only on
a low tide. Cross, turn when the tide is going down, come back, and fall
through to the passage, then cross it to the far refuge before it rises.
can kill you: the tide

## 18. The high bank  [combine: the geyser + a sword is a ledge]  floors 1 to 2
A jet that throws you a storey short of the bank, against a timber face.
At the top of the jet, throw into the timber. On the next eruption, ride up
and step off onto your sword, then up onto the bank, and recall it from
there.
can kill you: the lava
brazier: on the high bank

## 19. The lair stair  [breather]  floors 2 to 1
A long stair down. Claw marks on the walls and the heat getting stronger.
The exit is one way, into level 2.

# Before building (Claude's questions for Matt)
# 1. What does lava do to a sword? Nothing decides it today. Most beats here
#    put a miss over lava, so it is the stake of the whole level. Claude's
#    proposal: lava takes the sword, as a kill does. Matt's call.
# 2. The tide is not placeable yet. Only today's tide room has one, built by
#    hand. Building this needs a `tide` kind in the level format (its low
#    and high in cells, its clock in `config/hazards.tres`), in every level,
#    as lifts and geysers are.
# 3. Beat 18 needs a throw at the top of a jet. The code allows a throw in
#    the air when it is not a somersault, but no room has asked for one, and
#    whether a sword thrown there is a ledge you can then reach is a number
#    to measure on a bench before the beat is drawn.
# 4. The graveyard's swords (8a) must not read as swords to pick up, or the
#    one real sword there teaches you to distrust every sword you find
#    (`LEVELS.md`, *Surprises*). Snapped blades and hilts, never a whole one?
# 5. Two levels for Act 2, and this split? `SPEC.md` allows two or three.
# 6. Every species outside its room (`SPEC.md`, *Structure*): this sheet has
#    bats and one scorpion. An eyeball or an ant could go on 15 or 17 if
#    Matt wants a mixed group. Left out so each beat has one new thing in it.
